  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="&quot;80TH REGIMENT OF FOOT (STAFFORDSHIRE VOLUNTEERS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"80th Regiment of Foot (Staffordshire Volunteers) was an infantry regiment of the British Army, raised in 1793, and later amalgamated with the 38th (1st Staffordshire) Regiment of Foot to form the South Staffordshire Regiment."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0270-e7d976fc35f8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOUTH STAFFORDSHIRE REGIMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"South Staffordshire Regiment is the continuation of the lineage of the 80th Regiment of Foot (Staffordshire Volunteers) after the Childers Reforms in 1881."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0270-e7d976fc35f8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;3RD BATTALION, MERCIAN REGIMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"3rd Battalion, Mercian Regiment continues the lineage of the 80th Regiment of Foot (Staffordshire Volunteers)."&lt;SEP&gt;"3rd Battalion, Mercian Regiment continues the lineage of the 80th Regiment of Foot (Staffordshire Volunteers)."(</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0270-e7d976fc35f8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;93RD (SUTHERLAND HIGHLANDERS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"93rd (Sutherland Highlanders) is mentioned as part of a series of regiments, but specific details about its formation and activities are not provided in the given text."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0270-e7d976fc35f8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;94TH (ROYAL WELSH VOLUNTEERS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"94th (Royal Welsh Volunteers) is also part of a series of regiments, with no specific details provided in the given text."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0270-e7d976fc35f8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;95TH (RIFLEMEN)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"95th (Riflemen) is included in the series of regiments, but lacks detailed information in the provided text."&lt;SEP&gt;"95th (Riflemen) is included in the series of regiments, but lacks specific details in the provided text."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0270-e7d976fc35f8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;91ST (PRINCESS LOUISE'S ARGYLLSHIRE HIGHLANDERS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"91st (Princess Louise's Argyllshire Highlanders) is another regiment in the series, with no additional details provided."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0270-e7d976fc35f8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;92ND (DONEGAL LIGHT INFANTRY)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"92nd (Donegal Light Infantry) is part of the series, but lacks detailed information in the given text."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0270-e7d976fc35f8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THOMAS GAGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Thomas Gage was a colonel who raised the 80th Regiment of Light-Armed Foot in May 1758."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0270-e7d976fc35f8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LORD LOUDOUN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lord Loudoun was the commander-in-chief in North America and advised the adoption of regular officers and trusted men to combat the French and their allies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lord Loudoun was the commander-in-chief in North America following the advice of the Duke of Cumberland, who viewed the rangers as often unreliable and ill-disciplined."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0270-e7d976fc35f8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ROGER'S RANGERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Roger's Rangers were a group known for their tactics and equipment that influenced the formation of the 80th Regiment of Light-Armed Foot."&lt;SEP&gt;"Roger's Rangers were known for their reliability and effectiveness, providing proven tactics and equipment for the new regiment."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0270-e7d976fc35f8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FRENCH AND INDIAN WAR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The French and Indian War is the context in which the Regiment of Light-Armed Foot was formed to combat France and its Native American allies."&lt;SEP&gt;"The French and Indian War was a conflict during which the 80th Regiment of Light-Armed Foot was formed to combat France and its Native American allies."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0270-e7d976fc35f8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BRITISH ARMY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The British Army includes various regiments such as the 80th Regiment of Foot (Staffordshire Volunteers), 93rd (Sutherland Highlanders), 94th (Royal Welsh Volunteers), 95th (Riflemen), 91st (Princess Louise's Argyllshire Highlanders), 92nd (Donegal Light Infantry), and others."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0270-e7d976fc35f8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DUKE OF CUMBERLAND&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Duke of Cumberland advised Lord Loudoun on the reliability and discipline of the rangers, influencing the formation of the 80th Regiment of Light-Armed Foot."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Duke of Cumberland provided advice to Lord Loudoun regarding the formation of a reliable and disciplined regiment."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0270-e7d976fc35f8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NATIVE AMERICAN ALLIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Native American allies of France also required addressing during the French and Indian War, necessitating a formal regiment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Native American allies were part of the forces opposing the British Army, including the 80th Regiment of Foot (Staffordshire Volunteers), during the French and Indian War."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0270-e7d976fc35f8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FRANCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"France is mentioned as an adversary during the French and Indian War, requiring a formal regiment to combat."&lt;SEP&gt;"France was one of the adversaries of the British Army, particularly during the French and Indian War, which influenced the formation of regiments like the 80th Regiment of Foot (Staffordshire Volunteers&lt;SEP&gt;"France was one of the adversaries of the British Army, particularly during the French and Indian War, which influenced the formation of regiments like the 80th Regiment of Foot (Staffordshire Volunteers)."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0270-e7d976fc35f8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MAY 1758&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DATE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"May 1758 marks the formation date of the Regiment of Light-Armed Foot."&lt;SEP&gt;"The 80th Regiment of Light-Armed Foot was raised in May 1758."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0270-e7d976fc35f8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1793&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DATE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The 80th Regiment of Foot (Staffordshire Volunteers) was raised in 1793."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0270-e7d976fc35f8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;REGIMENT OF LIGHT-ARMED FOOT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Regiment of Light-Armed Foot was formed in May 1758 to combat France and its Native American allies during the French and Indian War, using tactics and equipment proven by Roger's Rangers."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0270-e7d976fc35f8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;73RD (HIGHLAND) REGIMENT OF FOOT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"73rd (Highland) Regiment of Foot was raised in 1780 as the 2nd Battalion of the 42nd (Highland) Regiment of Foot and later reconstituted as the 73rd Regiment of Foot in 1786."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0270-e7d976fc35f8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;74TH REGIMENT OF FOOT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"74th Regiment of Foot was raised in 1745 and later disbanded in 1746."&lt;SEP&gt;"74th Regiment of Foot was raised in 1745 as Lord Halifax's Regiment and disbanded in 1746."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0270-e7d976fc35f8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;2ND BATTALION, THE BLACK WATCH ROYAL REGIMENT OF SCOTLAND&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"2nd Battalion, The Black Watch Royal Regiment of Scotland was formed in 1881 from the 74th Regiment of Foot."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0270-e7d976fc35f8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ROGER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Roger is mentioned as the founder of Roger's Rangers, whose tactics and equipment were adopted by the new regiment."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0270-e7d976fc35f8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LORD HALIFAX'S REGIMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lord Halifax's Regiment was raised in 1745 and later became the 74th Regiment of Foot."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0270-e7d976fc35f8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;2ND BATTALION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"2nd Battalion refers to the second battalion of the 42nd (Highland) Regiment of Foot, which was reconstituted as the 73rd Regiment of Foot."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0270-e7d976fc35f8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;42ND (HIGHLAND) REGIMENT OF FOOT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"42nd (Highland) Regiment of Foot was the parent regiment from which the 73rd (Highland) Regiment of Foot was derived."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0270-e7d976fc35f8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BLACK WATCH ROYAL REGIMENT OF SCOTLAND&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Black Watch Royal Regiment of Scotland is the current name of the 2nd Battalion, which was formed from the 74th Regiment of Foot."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0270-e7d976fc35f8</data>
    </node>
